<%# /model_pipeline — EVERY CHARACTER MODEL IN FLIGHT, IN FIVE LANES.
    The operator's ask: "a similar swim lane to /deployments … a 1000 ft view of the
    models being generated." So this page is built to be SCANNED, not read: the lane a
    card sits in and the one sentence on it are the whole interface, and every control
    that would spend money lives on the model page a card links to.

    REBASED ON THE ENGINE PRIMITIVE, not a second board. studio/board/board owns the
    SortableJS drag, the cross-lane PATCH, the rank POST, the counts and the toasts;
    Appearance carries Studio::Board::Rankable and ModelPipelineController includes
    Studio::Board::Reorderable. This wrapper owns no JavaScript of its own — there is no
    per-card write on this board, because a drag triggers nothing.

    A NON-ADMIN GETS A READ-ONLY BOARD BY CONSTRUCTION: with no move_url and no
    reorder_url the factory reverts a cross-lane drop and posts nothing, so the public
    read cannot produce a refused write it has no way to act on. %>
<% board = @board %>
<% draggable = admin? %>

<section class="min-h-screen space-y-6">
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-end justify-between gap-3">
    <div class="min-w-0">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-heading">Model Pipeline</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Every character model in flight. A lane is where a model's own evidence puts it.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
      <span class="badge text-2xs <%= pipeline_chip_classes(:neutral) %>" data-test="pipeline-total">
        <%= pluralize(board[:total], "model") %>
      </span>
      <% if board[:stale_count].positive? %>
        <span class="badge text-2xs <%= pipeline_chip_classes(:bad) %>" data-test="pipeline-stale-count">
          <%= board[:stale_count] %> need re-defining
        </span>
      <% end %>
      <% if board[:hand_placed_count].positive? %>
        <span class="badge text-2xs <%= pipeline_chip_classes(:info) %>" data-test="pipeline-hand-placed-count">
          <%= board[:hand_placed_count] %> placed by hand
        </span>
      <% end %>
      <%= link_to "People →", people_path, class: "btn btn-sm btn-outline" %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# ── THE TWO RULES THIS BOARD RUNS ON ──────────────────────────────────────────
      Stated on the page rather than in a comment, because both are answers to
      questions the operator will ask the first time a card does not go where he put
      it, and a board that cannot explain itself sends him to read Ruby. %>
  <div class="card p-4 space-y-3" data-test="pipeline-legend">
    <p class="label-upper text-primary">How the lanes move</p>
    <dl class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <dt class="text-xs font-bold text-heading">Dragging a card triggers nothing.</dt>
        <dd class="text-2xs text-secondary leading-snug">
          A drag records where you put it and the order of the lane. It never searches,
          classifies, mints or generates — nothing on this board spends money. The
          controls that do live on each model's own page.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt class="text-xs font-bold text-heading">A hand placement moves a model forward, never back.</dt>
        <dd class="text-2xs text-secondary leading-snug">
          Lanes are derived from what a model has. You can drag a card ahead of its
          evidence and it stays there; dragging it behind is refused, so the board can
          never show less progress than the work that has actually been done. A change
          in the person's data — a trade — sets your placement aside and the card says so.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
    <p class="text-2xs text-muted border-t border-subtle pt-2" data-test="pipeline-definition-gap">
      <%= Appearances::Pipeline::DEFINITION_GAP_NOTE %>
    </p>
  </div>

  <%# The board. Columns are the five lanes; each card is model_pipeline/_look_card,
      bound to :reading. A cross-lane drop PATCHes { appearance: { stage } } to
      #update; a reorder POSTs the DOM-ordered slugs to the shared reorder action. No
      live channel — nothing broadcasts a look yet, and a channel with no publisher is
      furniture. %>
  <%= render "studio/board/board",
        columns: board[:lanes].map { |lane|
          {
            key: lane.key,
            label: lane.label,
            cards: lane.cards,
            count: lane.total,
            count_class: lane_count_classes(lane.key),
            min_width: "sm:min-w-[210px]",
            kickoff: lane_blurb_slot(lane),
            header_extra: lane_overflow_chip(lane)
          }
        },
        card_partial: "model_pipeline/look_card",
        card_as: :reading,
        card_locals: { draggable: draggable },
        reorder_url: (draggable ? reorder_model_pipeline_path(format: :json) : nil),
        reorder_payload: :slugs,
        move_url: (draggable ? "/model_pipeline/:id.json" : nil),
        move_param: (draggable ? { resource: :appearance, attr: :stage } : nil),
        group: "model-pipeline",
        id_attr: "slug",
        zone_attr: "stage",
        live_channel: nil,
        toasts: true,
        empty_label: "No models here" %>
</section>
